<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Albany, New York</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Albany is the capital of the state of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a>, on the west bank of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hudson-river">Hudson River</a>. It grew from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> fur-trading post of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fort-orange">Fort Orange</a>, built in 1624 near an earlier post of 1614, and the village of Beverwijck. After the English conquest of 1664 it was renamed after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/james-ii-of-england">James, Duke of York</a> and Albany; it was chartered as a city in 1686 and became the state capital in 1797.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/albany-new-york.jpg" alt="Albany, New York" width="320" height="192" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Quintin Soloviev · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Albany,_New_York.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Some 4,000 British immigrants, the 1820 Settlers, were placed in the <b>Albany</b> district of the Eastern Cape, and English replaced Dutch as the language of government and courts in the 1820s.</blockquote><a href="/empire/cape-colony">Cape Colony · Socioeconomy</a></li><li><blockquote>The Mohawk traded beaver pelts with the Dutch at Fort Orange, founded in 1624 on the site of present-day <b>Albany</b>, for metal tools, cloth and firearms, and later traded with the English.</blockquote><a href="/empire/iroquois-confederacy">Iroquois Confederacy · Socioeconomy</a></li><li><blockquote>Alexander Hamilton, who served as George Washington's aide in the Revolutionary War, married Elizabeth Schuyler at the Schuyler Mansion in <b>Albany, New York</b>.</blockquote><a href="/today-in-history/december-14">14 December in history</a></li></ul></section>
